 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>Consider the set of generation I legendary Pokémon, <span data-math=\"L = \\{ {\\text{Articuno, Zapdos, Moltres, Mewtwo}}\\} \">L = \\{ {\\text{Articuno, Zapdos, Moltres, Mewtwo}}\\} </span>. Give an example of a proper subset containing:</p>\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 494315,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "one member.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A set is a proper subset of <i>L</i> if every member of the subset is a member of <i>L</i> and the subset does <i>not</i> contain an element that is in <i>L</i>. The proper subsets of <i>L</i> with one member include the following.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\{\\rm Articuno\\}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\{\\rm Zapdos\\}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\{\\rm Moltres\\}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\{\\rm Mewtwo\\}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>A set with one member could contain any one of the following:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\{ {\\text{Articuno}}\\} {\\text{, }}\\{ {\\text{Zapdos}}\\} {\\text{, }}\\{ {\\text{Moltres}}\\} {\\text{, or }}\\{ {\\text{Mewtwo}}\\} \">\\{ {\\text{Articuno}}\\} {\\text{, }}\\{ {\\text{Zapdos}}\\} {\\text{, }}\\{ {\\text{Moltres}}\\} {\\text{, or }}\\{ {\\text{Mewtwo}}\\}</span>.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 494316,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "three members.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A set is a proper subset of <i>L</i> if every member of the subset is a member of <i>L</i> and the subset does <i>not</i> contain an element that is in <i>L</i>. The proper subsets of <i>L</i> with three members will include three elements and leave out one.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\{\\rm Articuno,\\ Zapdos,\\ Moltres\\}\"></span>\n</p><p><span data-math=\"\\{\\rm Articuno,\\ Zapdos,\\ Mewtwo\\}\"></span>\n</p><p><span data-math=\"\\{\\rm Articuno,\\ Moltres,\\ Mewtwo\\}\"></span>\n</p><p><span data-math=\"\\{\\rm Zapdos,\\ Moltres,\\ Mewtwo\\}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>Any of the following combinations of three members would work:</p> \n<p><span data-math=\"\\{ {\\text{Articuno, Zapdos, Mewtwo}}\\} \">\\{ {\\text{Articuno, Zapdos, Mewtwo}}\\}</span>,<span data-math=\"\\{ {\\text{Articuno, Moltres, Mewtwo}}\\} \">\\{ {\\text{Articuno, Moltres, Mewtwo}}\\}</span>, or <span data-math=\"\\{ {\\text{Zapdos, Moltres, Mewtwo}}\\} \">\\{ {\\text{Zapdos, Moltres, Mewtwo}}\\}</span>.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 494317,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "no members.",
   "answers": [],
